<title>PORTUGAL: BPI issues 15 bln esc perpetual bonds.</title>
<headline>BPI issues 15 bln esc perpetual bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Portugues de Investimento (BPI) is issuing 15 billion escudos of perpetual bonds subordinated to three-month Lisbor plus 70 basis points (bp) in the first seven years, BPI said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The issue, which is led by Banco Cisf, is intended to finance BPI's recent acquisition of Banco do Fomento e Exterior (BFE).</p>
<p>&quot;This is the first issue of this kind in Portugal,&quot; BPI said.</p>
<p>Payment date is December 18.</p>
</text>
